  data: {
    LLM: "Use the Case Keeper religiously. Never bet on an 'exhausted' card (one that has all 4 remaining cards drawn). This single rule eliminates most losing propositions.\n\n**Split Probability**: As the deck thins, calculate the likelihood of splits. If only one 5 remains in the deck, a 5-5 split is impossibleâ€”bets on 5 become slightly favored. Conversely, if multiple cards of the same rank remain, splits become more likely, worsening odds on those ranks. **Coppering Strategy**: Copper bets on ranks where you believe a specific card is about to be drawn as the Loser first.\n\n**Deck State Analysis**: Track not just which ranks remain but which specific suits remain. Some dealing boxes may show card orientation, hinting at suit. **Bet Sizing**: Use the Case Keeper to identify the single turning (3-card ending) opportunityâ€”this is the only time an exotic 4:1 bet becomes favorable. **Martingale Rejection**: Resist the temptation to use the Martingale system (doubling bets after losses). Faro's random nature makes all betting systems statistically unreliable long-term.",
    Player: "Use the Case Keeper religiously. Never bet on an 'exhausted' card (one that has all 4 remaining cards drawn). This single rule eliminates most losing propositions.\n\n**Split Probability**: As the deck thins, calculate the likelihood of splits. If only one 5 remains in the deck, a 5-5 split is impossibleâ€”bets on 5 become slightly favored. Conversely, if multiple cards of the same rank remain, splits become more likely, worsening odds on those ranks. **Coppering Strategy**: Copper bets on ranks where you believe a specific card is about to be drawn as the Loser first.\n\n**Deck State Analysis**: Track not just which ranks remain but which specific suits remain. Some dealing boxes may show card orientation, hinting at suit. **Bet Sizing**: Use the Case Keeper to identify the single turning (3-card ending) opportunityâ€”this is the only time an exotic 4:1 bet becomes favorable. **Martingale Rejection**: Resist the temptation to use the Martingale system (doubling bets after losses). Faro's random nature makes all betting systems statistically unreliable long-term.",
